  "question": {
    "text": "The range of the function $f(x)=\\sqrt{3 x^2-4 x+5}$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Iv7nT",
      "text": " $\\left(-\\infty, \\sqrt{\\frac{11}{3}}\\right]$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "e5Vxe",
      "text": "$\\left(-\\infty, \\sqrt{\\frac{11}{5}}\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "urlEk",
      "text": "$\\left[\\sqrt{\\frac{11}{3}}, \\infty\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "LQAst",
      "text": "$\\left(\\sqrt{\\frac{11}{5}}, \\infty\\right)$.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$f(x)$ is defined if $3 x^2-4 x+5 \\geq 0$<br />$\\Rightarrow 3\\left[x^2-\\frac{4}{3} x+\\frac{5}{3}\\right] \\geq 0 \\Rightarrow 3\\left[\\left(x-\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^2+\\frac{11}{9}\\right] \\geq 0$<br />Which is true for all real $x \\therefore$ Domain of $f(x)=$ $(-\\infty, \\infty)$<br />Let $y=\\sqrt{3 x^2-4 x+5}$<br />$\\Rightarrow y^2=3 x^2-4 x+5$ i.e. $3 x^2-4 x+\\left(5-y^2\\right)=0$<br />For $x$ to be real , $16-12\\left(5-y^2\\right) \\geq 0 \\Rightarrow y \\geq \\sqrt{\\frac{11}{3}}$<br />$\\therefore \\quad$ Range of $y=\\left[\\sqrt{\\frac{11}{3}}, \\infty\\right)$",
    "image": null
  },
